.TH BAM 1 "December 2025" "1.0" "Barakadax Audio Manager Manual"

.SH NAME
bam \- Barakadax Audio Manager

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bam
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bam
is a simple yet powerful audio manager for Linux, built with GTK 4. It allows you to:
.IP \[bu] 2
Control volume for individual output devices.
.IP \[bu]
Set the default output device.
.IP \[bu]
View and manage audio streams associated with running processes.
.IP \[bu]
"Drop" (stop) an audio stream by double-clicking its Process ID (PID) in the list or dragging it.
.IP \[bu]
Drag-and-drop process streams to different output devices.

The interface features a modern "Liquid Glass" aesthetic with transparency and blur effects.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Display this help and exit. (Note: standard GTK help may appear)

.SH FILES
.TP
.I src/style.css
Defines the visual style of the application.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bam/
Configuration files (if any in future versions).

